---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/layout/Section.astro";
import Container from "../components/layout/Container.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
import ClassifiedBand from "../components/ui/ClassifiedBand.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/typography/Eyebrow.astro";
import Heading from "../components/typography/Heading.astro";
import Rule from "../components/typography/Rule.astro";
import PitchDeckNav from "@/components/ui/PitchDeckNav.astro";
import ProfileCard from "@/components/characters/ProfileCard.astro";
import ProfileSection from "@/components/characters/ProfileSection.astro";
import AgentList from "@/components/characters/AgentList.astro";
import "@/styles/global.css";
import ThreatBand from "@/components/ui/ThreatBand.astro";

// @TODO: wrap in new PitchDeckLayout, replacing Layout
// @TODO: see if SmallProfileCard can be used here or integrated with ProfileCard
---

<Layout title="MI5 Monitoring Station — Core Frequency Anomaly">
  <ClassifiedBand
    label="TOP SECRET — MI5 MONITORING STATION // CORE FREQUENCY ANOMALY"
  />

  <!-- ─── PAGE HEADER ─── -->
  <Section variant="black" spacing="md">
    <Container>
      <Eyebrow>Central Collision</Eyebrow>
      <Heading level={2} variant="section">The <em>Battleground</em></Heading>
      <Rule />
      <p class="prose page-intro">
        The ultimate absurd ideological showdown. Working-class chaos against
        centuries of royal choreography. A rebellion that isn't really a
        rebellion. An institution that isn't even paying attention.
      </p>
      <ThreatBand line1="MI5 MONITORING STATOIN // CORE FREQUENCY ANOMALY" line2="THE REBELLION VS. THE CROWN" />
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <Section variant="black" spacing="md">
    <div class="collision-grid">
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <!-- JOHN LENNON — LEFT -->
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <ProfileCard
        variant="lennon"
        photo="/john.jpg"
        photoAlt="John Lennon — 1965"
        photoLabel="ABBEY ROAD // RECORDING TAPE BOX"
        badge="THE REBELLION"
        name="JOHN LENNON"
        subtitle="// The Unintentional Anarchist"
        quote="We are where we are, lads. Best be relaxed. We're about to get medals. I mean, they're honors for pop music. It's not like we actually had to kill anyone to get them."
        style="background: var(--bg-subtle); padding: 4rem; border: 1px solid var(--red-text-subtle); border-right: none;"
      >
        <ProfileSection label="The Stance">
          <p>
            Slouching, irreverent, and chemically relaxed. Armed with a
            working-class Liverpool wit, a packed joint in his velvet jacket
            pocket, and an instinctive disdain for institutional pretension.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Threat Profile">
          <p>
            <strong>High Cultural Authority.</strong> John isn't trying to overthrow
            the government; he's just naturally skeptical of royal pomp. But to a
            rigid establishment, his casual, effortless influence over millions of
            youth makes him look more dangerous than an army of foreign agents.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Comedy DNA">
          <AgentList
            items={[
              {
                term: "The Unwitting Catalyst",
                body: `John's "killing people" comment at the MBE ceremony is pure
               working-class irreverence, not calculated political protest.
               He has no idea he just made the most powerful enemy of his life.`,
              },
              {
                term: "The Inverse Feedback Loop",
                body: `Every MI5 manipulation designed to destroy him — the "Jesus"
               controversy amplification, the media hostility, the institutional
               pressure — pushes him further into radicalization. The conspiracy
               creates the very threat it was designed to neutralize.`,
              },
              {
                term: "The Accidental Radical",
                body: `His genuine political awakening — driven by authentic conviction
               and primal therapy — is also partially the product of the very
               conspiracy designed to destroy him. Dramatic irony as the engine
               of tragedy.`,
              },
            ]}
          />
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Trajectory">
          <p>
            Stumbles into a multi-year psychological war he doesn't know he's
            fighting. Every time MI5 tries to subtle-sabotage him, his music
            just gets sharper, weirder, and more radicalized — culminating in
            the ultimate act of defiance: returning his actual MBE medal to
            Buckingham Palace.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Internal Conflict">
          <p>
            Torn between his desire for peace and his naturally combative
            personality. He preaches love and understanding while being quick to
            anger and harsh judgment. This contradiction makes him vulnerable —
            he genuinely wants to make the world better but his methods often
            alienate the very people he needs to reach. He's caught between
            loyalty to The Beatles (his artistic family) and his growing need
            for individual expression. Every choice that serves his personal
            growth seems to damage the band, creating guilt he masks with
            defiance.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Vulnerabilities">
          <p>
            Abandonment anxiety (father left, mother died, band fracturing).
            Impostor syndrome despite massive success. Susceptible to paranoia
            when under pressure. Self-destructive tendencies when feeling
            trapped. And a deep-seated need for authenticity in an increasingly
            artificial world — a need that makes him both impossible to control
            and dangerously predictable to those who understand it.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>

        <ProfileSection label="The Narrative Arc — Three Acts">
          <AgentList
            items={[
              {
                term: "1965 — The Unwitting Catalyst",
                body: `John's casual "killing people" quip at the MBE ceremony is pure
               instinct, not rebellion. His casual disrespect unknowingly triggers
               Philip's five-year vendetta.`,
              },
              {
                term: "1968 — The Manipulated Radical",
                body: `Operation Minuet's psychological campaign amplifies every
               controversy around him. He becomes the radical Philip needs him
               to be.`,
              },
              {
                term: "1970 — The Defiant Survivor",
                body: `Returns his MBE. Survives an assassination attempt he never
               knows about. He walks away free, never learning how close he
               came to death.`,
              },
            ]}
          />
        </ProfileSection>
      </ProfileCard>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <!-- THE QUEEN — RIGHT -->
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
      <ProfileCard
        variant="crown"
        photo="/queen.jpg"
        photoAlt="Queen Elizabeth - 1960's"
        photoLabel="BUCKINGHAM PALACE // OFFICIAL PORTRAIT"
        badge="HER MAJESTY THE QUEEN"
        name="Queen Elizabeth"
        subtitle="// The Oblivious Institution"
        quote="They seem like very polite young men, Philip. The short one with the drums has a lovely smile. Do stop pacing, you're making the corgis anxious."
        style="background: var(--bg-subtle); padding: 4rem; border: 1px solid var(--red-text-subtle); border-left: none;"
      >
        <ProfileSection label="The Stance">
          <p>
            Perfectly poised, completely unbothered, and utterly detached from
            the panic brewing in her own basement. Armed with inherited
            centuries of tradition, absolute social grace, and a genuine
            indifference to rock-and-roll.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Threat Profile">
          <p>
            <strong> Absolute Institutional Weight. </strong>
            She represents the massive, immovable iceberg of the British Empire. She
            doesn't dislike the Beatles; she graciously hands them their medals because
            her Prime Minister told her to.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Grand Satirical Irony">
          <p>
            The Queen is the epic center of the show's cosmic joke. While Prince
            Philip uses the entire apparatus of MI5 to protect her honor from
            Lennon's "rebellion," Her Majesty remains blissfully unaware of the
            multi-million dollar conspiracy operating in her name. She treats
            the Beatles like a passing weather system, entirely blind to the
            fact that her husband has turned her palace into a paranoid cold-war
            command center.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Comedy DNA">
          <AgentList
            items={[
              {
                term: "The Oblivious Iceberg",
                body: `The Queen is the massive, immovable institution — while Philip rages and Mountbatten schemes downstairs, 
                  she's signing state papers and asking about the corgis. The entire conspiracy operates in a building whose owner
                  has no idea it exists.`,
              },
              {
                term: "The Flat Arc",
                body: `She maintains absolute consistency while
                everyone around her spirals. Her presence at Committee meetings serves
                as both legitimacy and restraint — she contributes hilariously mundane
                counterpoints to Mountbatten's psychological warfare briefings (questioning
                budgets, suggesting tea service protocols).`,
              },
              {
                term: "The Final Judgment",
                body: `Her one scene of moral weight — a look, not a speech — delivers the series' verdict. Patience defeats everything. The institution endures not by acting, but by refusing to.`,
              },
            ]}
          />
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Motivation">
          <p>
            Her overriding motivation is <strong
              >institutional preservation</strong
            >. She views the monarchy as a thousand-year institution that must
            outlast any individual crisis, including her husband's wounded
            pride. John's 1965 comment is, to her, a momentary irritation that
            will be forgotten if ignored, but could become a lasting scandal if
            mishandled. Her secondary motivation is managing Philip's escalating
            obsession — by participating in the Committee, she hopes to moderate
            his impulses and prevent actions that could genuinely threaten the
            Crown.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Internal Conflict">
          <p>
            Torn between duty to her husband and duty to the Crown. She is loyal
            to Philip and feels a deep, if formal, affection for him. But his
            Operation Minuet runs counter to her every instinct for caution and
            stability. Every time she reluctantly sanctions a part of his plan,
            she weighs the risk of indulging his folly against the risk of
            directly opposing him and causing a domestic crisis. She is a
            fundamentally conservative individual forced to oversee a radically
            unconventional and undignified operation. Her struggle is to
            maintain the dignity of her office while being party to something
            utterly lacking in it.
          </p>
        </ProfileSection>
        <ProfileSection label="The Narrative Arc - Three Acts">
          <AgentList
            items={[
              {
                term: "1965 — The Cautious Voice",
                body: "Witnesses John's comment with diplomatic composure. When Philip convenes the Committee, she participates reluctantly, hoping her presence will moderate his response. 'He's an artist, Philip. They're meant to be dramatic.'",
              },
              {
                term: "1968 — The Reluctant Moderator",
                body: "Serves as the Committee's conscience. Her contributions are hilariously mundane — questioning budgets, suggesting protocol. Watches Philip's growing obsession with increasing concern.",
              },
              {
                term: "1970 — The Vindicated Survivor",
                body: "John's MBE return triggers Philip's assassination demand. Her horror represents her moral line. When the plot collapses into farce, her reaction is weary vindication. Her final look to Philip reaffirms: institutions endure by staying above personal vendettas.",
              },
            ]}
          />
        </ProfileSection>
      </ProfileCard>

      <!-- ─── CENTER OVERLAP STAMP ─── -->
      <div class="center-stamp" aria-hidden="true">
        CULTURAL CONTAGION DIRECTIVE<br />
        <span class="stamp-sub">DO NOT CROSS FILE</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <!-- ─── DIAGNOSTIC SUMMARY ─────────── -->
  <Section variant="paper" spacing="md" style="max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <Container>
      <Eyebrow>Diagnostic Summary</Eyebrow>
      <Heading level={2} variant="section"
        >The Anatomy of an <em>Irreverent Farce</em></Heading
      >
      <Rule />

      <div class="diagnostic-band">
        <pre
          class="diagnostic-header">
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DIAGNOSTIC SUMMARY // THE ANATOMY OF AN IRREVERENT FARCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        </pre>
      </div>

      <h4 class="diag-subhead">The Ideological Cold War</h4>

      <p class="prose">
        This is the comedy of <strong>asymmetric warfare</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="asymmetric-grid">
        <div class="asymmetric-item">
          <span class="asymmetric-char asymmetric-char--lennon">Lennon</span>
          <p>
            fights a very loud, very public battle against the concept of "The
            Establishment."
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="asymmetric-item">
          <span class="asymmetric-char asymmetric-char--queen">The Queen</span>
          <p>
            <em>is</em> the establishment, but she is too busy reviewing state paperwork
            and managing royal lineages to notice his protest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="prose">
        The real conflict is fought entirely in the shadow between them. Prince
        Philip and his bumbling agents treat a pop band's lyrics like a matter
        of imperial national security, launching a secret war against a
        counter-culture movement that doesn't even know it's under attack. It is
        the ultimate collision of working-class chaos against centuries of royal
        choreography.
      </p>
    </Container>
  </Section>

  <PitchDeckNav current="/collision" />
  <!-- ─── FOOTER ─── -->
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ─── PAGE INTRO ─── */
  .page-intro {
    max-width: 650px;
    color: var(--text5);
    font-size: var(--fs4);
    margin: var(--space-1);
  }

  /* ─── MONITORING BAND ─── */
  .monitoring-band {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: var(--space-1) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bg4);
  }

  .monitoring-header {
    max-width: var(--container-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--accent-blue);
    letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─── COLLISION GRID ─── */
  .collision-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ─── CENTER STAMP ─── */
  .center-stamp {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(-15deg);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs1);
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.4;
    padding: 12px 24px;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-red);
    color: var(--color-red);
    background: rgba(139, 26, 26, 0.08);
    z-index: 10;
    pointer-events: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .stamp-sub {
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ─── DIAGNOSTIC SECTION ─── */
  .diagnostic-band {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
  }

  .diagnostic-header {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.04rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-faint);
    padding: var(--space-3);
    background: var(--bg2);
  }

  .diag-subhead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text2);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .asymmetric-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
  }

  .asymmetric-item {
    background: var(--bg2);
    padding: var(--space-4);
  }

  .asymmetric-item:first-child {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .asymmetric-item:last-child {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-amber);
  }

  .asymmetric-char {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }

  .asymmetric-char--lennon {
    color: var(--accent-blue);
  }

  .asymmetric-char--queen {
    color: var(--color-amber);
  }

  .asymmetric-item p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text5);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ─── RESPONSIVE ─── */
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .collision-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .collision-panel--lennon {
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bg);
    }

    .center-stamp {
      position: relative;
      top: auto;
      left: auto;
      transform: rotate(-8deg);
      margin: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 0.7rem;
    }

    .asymmetric-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .photo-label {
      font-size: 0.45rem;
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .center-stamp {
      transform: rotate(-5deg);
      font-size: 0.6rem;
      padding: 8px 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
